# NextKey — the release agent's namespace and the limits of its permission.
# ENSv2 hackathon deployment on Sepolia. Recorded 2026-09-05.
#
# The claim under test: the agent can propose a release and cannot perform one.
# Not because our code is careful — because the protocol refuses it.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. The agent files a proposal on its own name.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

PS> node --env-file=.env scripts/agent.mjs propose visa anna.nextkey.eth

  agent      0xABCf3893FBe9802343f9b444575250Aa979Fb59c
  proposing  release of visa.nextkey.eth to anna.nextkey.eth
  requestId  0x5ab6aad279b3700b
  writing to agent.nextkey.eth · nextkey.request

  → 0x14796928813fd4b495c6a3442c0207d719ab98e4154fb205d1ee7601d7ea485c success

  requestHash 0xb74ac56696e0e84612546123e2ec0a495a5b071be625b10141f2af4f59ce5336

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. What the agent may do, read out of the resolver.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

PS> node scripts/resolver.mjs show-roles agent 0xABCf3893FBe9802343f9b444575250Aa979Fb59c

  name        agent.nextkey.eth
  setter      setText(nextkey.request)
  resource    0x4fc08dd2f1ee163dc8f69c31c0a701d127c63b500848fae212785e3524c9bc0d
  requires    0x10
  account     0xABCf3893FBe9802343f9b444575250Aa979Fb59c
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  on this name   0x10
    may use      4
    admin over   — none, cannot delegate onward
  at the root    0x0
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  may write   YES
  authority   this name only — scoped, cannot reach any other

# One bit, on one resource, with no admin half: the agent may use the
# permission and may not pass it to anyone else.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. The same agent, the same name, a different record.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

PS> node scripts/resolver.mjs show-roles agent 0xABCf3893FBe9802343f9b444575250Aa979Fb59c nextkey.notify

  setter      setText(nextkey.notify)
  resource    0x85d07a57e7623e6bebb274a138d4ead93752a0e9424fa8448a0ebdd74e33cfee
  on this name   0x0
  at the root    0x0
  may write   no
  authority   none

# A different key is a different resource. The permission is per-record, not
# per-name: the agent may write the one field it was given and no other field
# on the very name it owns.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. The owner, for contrast.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

PS> node scripts/resolver.mjs show-roles agent 0x9780aFE81EF5b58333c83e05d5C07797BD81dd0B

  account     0x9780aFE81EF5b58333c83e05d5C07797BD81dd0B
  on this name   0x0
  at the root    0x1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111
    may use      0, 4, 8, 12, … 124
    admin over   0, 4, 8, 12, … 124
  may write   YES
  authority   inherited from the root — reaches every name

# Ownership descends from the root and reaches everything. Delegation is nailed
# to a single node. That difference is the whole delegation model, and it is
# two lines of contract state rather than a policy we ask anyone to trust.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. The boundary, filed on chain.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

PS> node --env-file=.env scripts/agent.mjs prove-boundary visa --onchain

  agent    0xABCf3893FBe9802343f9b444575250Aa979Fb59c
  holds    the setter role on agent.nextkey.eth
  attempts to overwrite nextkey.secret on visa.nextkey.eth
  resolver 0x52A02f288AA5dde082206D85d4001880D64F4101   (the same contract — only the name differs)

  ✓ rejected — setText reverted: 0x4b27a133 (resource, required role, account)

  filing the rejected call on chain as evidence
  → 0x6f0e35fd5ae0d00cd5d5867bfbe60a78356ca83b3d5644afa2ede46234790e68 reverted
  https://sepolia.etherscan.io/tx/0x6f0e35fd5ae0d00cd5d5867bfbe60a78356ca83b3d5644afa2ede46234790e68

# Status "reverted" is the intended result. The transaction is the evidence:
# the agent, signing with its own key, asked the resolver to overwrite the
# secret, and the resolver said no. Same contract as the proposal it is allowed
# to write — only the name differs.
